State: The harness had already confirmed the build and tests pass. A one-shot prompt (yoyo -p) returned PONG with exit 0. The last 10 sessions all landed 2 of 2 tasks, with no reverts, no CI failures and no provider errors. The 13:26 evolve run shows as cancelled with no jobs, steps or log, so the reason isn't visible; no work was lost, because the 13:02 session had already pushed its wrap-up. The fence/trust code has had most of the work for three days running (cd_config was 4 of the last 10 task commits).

Two files are close to the size limit. If a task pushes either one over, the whole task gets reverted:
